<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    
    <!-- Enable Razor Class Library features -->
    <AddRazorSupportForMvc>true</AddRazorSupportForMvc>
    <GenerateEmbeddedFilesManifest>true</GenerateEmbeddedFilesManifest>
    
    <!-- This is a packable library -->
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    
    <!-- NuGet Package Metadata -->
    <PackageId>Manifesto.RazorKit</PackageId>
    <Version>0.3.0</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>0.3.0: theming, mobile support and accessibility. Upgrade by bumping the package version; no code changes are required.
- Themes: configure RazorKitOptions.Themes (a list of Name and DataTheme) to get a theme dropdown in the toolbar; the preview is rendered with data-theme set to the chosen theme. The choice is kept in the URL (?theme=) and remembered in the browser. With no themes configured the preview sets no theme. The old built-in "charity" default theme is removed: if your site relied on it, add it to RazorKitOptions.Themes.
- Mobile: on narrow screens the component list and the Controls panel become slide-out panels (one open at a time) and the preview uses the device width.
- Accessibility: RazorKit's own interface now uses real buttons, keyboard navigation, visible focus, labelled controls and improved contrast (working towards WCAG 2.2 AA).
- Edits in the Controls panel now survive viewport and theme changes.
- "Open in new window" opens the current, edited preview in a new tab.
- A single reset button ("Reset to story values", or "Reset to defaults" when the story sets no values) replaces the two previous ones.
- When a preview is refused (for example too many requests), the preview area shows a short readable message.
- GET previews now count towards the render concurrency limit (MaxConcurrentRenders), and viewport or theme changes with edited values count as renders.
- RazorKit's page script and styles are now served as package files rather than inline, so a host Content-Security-Policy no longer needs to allow inline script for RazorKit's page (inline styles are still used).
- Fixed: editing a story in the Controls panel (or switching viewport or theme) no longer breaks components whose props are typed as an interface or object.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>Manifesto Digital</Authors>
    <Company>Manifesto Digital</Company>
    <Description>A component preview and development tool for ASP.NET Core Razor components. Provides an interactive UI for developing, testing, and documenting reusable Razor components, inspired by Storybook.</Description>
    <PackageTags>razor;components;storybook;preview;development;aspnetcore;manifesto</PackageTags>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/manifesto-digital/razorkit</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/manifesto-digital/razorkit</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    
    <!-- Generate symbols package for debugging -->
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    
    <!-- The test project lives under this folder; keep its sources out of the package -->
    <DefaultItemExcludes>$(DefaultItemExcludes);tests/**</DefaultItemExcludes>

    <!-- Suppress warnings -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS8604</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Razor.RuntimeCompilation" Version="8.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net9.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Razor.RuntimeCompilation" Version="9.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Razor.RuntimeCompilation" Version="10.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Manifesto.RazorKit.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
